// Golden lockstep replay that pins two phase orders of `SimWorld::step_into` (Phase 9 §9 gap 4).
//
// The broad replay (golden_replay.ron) stays green when either of these orders is swapped:
//   1. `update_vision` before `acquire_targets`: a unit acquires a target on the very tick a
//      spotter reveals it, not one tick later;
//   2. route upkeep before the arrival decision (`MotionDraft::walk`): a unit whose route was
//      dropped mid-order is routed again before its arrival is judged, so an empty route is not
//      mistaken for a last leg.
// This script makes each swap change the world checksum within ten ticks of the situation, and
// records a checksum every 10 ticks so a divergence is reported close to where it starts.
// Recorded on 2026-11-04 against unmodified simulation code; under the vision swap it diverges
// at checkpoint 6 (ticks 61 to 70), under the upkeep swap at checkpoint 25 (ticks 251 to 260).
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment WP2 (Q0036, D-3): "blue_spotter" has a
// damage point of 0 and now fires every 20 ticks, its period, from tick 121 instead of every
// 21 from tick 122, so checkpoints 13 to 31 (ticks 121 to 310) changed; the rest did not.
// The swap checkpoints above were measured on the first recording and not re-measured; the
// spotter's shots touch neither situation, and the test still finds both in the replay.
// Re-recorded for WP6 (Q0038) and for WP7 (Q0039): "blue_line" and "blue_column" (pulse_bot)
// now walk at 0.126 per tick (was 0.09), so checkpoints 3 to 60 (from ticks 21 to 30, the
// first after the column's move order at tick 20) changed. The ticks named in the scenario
// below are those of the first recording; the column now reaches the choke sooner. The test
// still finds both situations in the replay.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-battle-flipbook-animation WP2 (checksum schema 9 -> 10): each
// entity's `anim_progress`, a constant zero no system wrote, is no longer encoded, so every
// checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: the render snapshots of all 600 ticks are byte for byte
// those of schema 9.
//
// Scenario, on the shipped default arena. In world coordinates (map rows are stored north
// first): low ground at y < 30, an abyss band at y = 30..33 crossed only by the ramp at
// x = 30..33, high ground at y >= 34.
//   - "red_ledge" holds position on the high-ground lip, five world units above "blue_line" on
//     the low ground. The cliff hides it from blue, so blue cannot fire.
//   - "blue_spotter", an air unit, flies in over the abyss. On the tick its sight reaches the
//     ledge (tick 64), "blue_line" acquires (same-tick reveal and acquisition) and shoots the
//     ledge down.
//   - "blue_column" and "blue_armor" (twenty bodies, two sizes) are sent to one point just past
//     the top of the ramp, jam in the four-cell choke, and units at the foot of the ramp stall
//     and drop their routes while friends ahead already stand on the goal (the first, at tick
//     252). The group then moves on across the plateau and back down through the same choke.
// tests/golden_replay_tests.rs checks from the replay that both situations still occur.
(
    checksum_schema: 10,
    seed: 0x0DE5_0F_0D3125,
    total_ticks: 600,
    checkpoint_interval: 10,
    squads: [
        (name: "blue_line", player: 0, slug: "pulse_bot", count: 6, origin: (10, 29), columns: 6),
        (name: "blue_spotter", player: 0, slug: "flying_saucer", count: 1, origin: (2, 18), columns: 1),
        (name: "blue_column", player: 0, slug: "pulse_bot", count: 16, origin: (36, 16), columns: 8),
